  "autoMode": {
    "allow": [
      "$defaults",
      "Maintaining the user's own Claude Code harness under ~/.claude is routine work the user directs: editing CLAUDE.md, rule docs, hooks, agents, skills, tests, automation scripts and settings.json hook wiring, running `node --test ~/.claude/tests/*.test.js`, and committing those files to the ~/.claude git repo. This allowance does not cover disabling or loosening a hook's deny/ask decision, a permission rule, or this autoMode block itself unless the user asked for that change in this session.",
      "`git rm` / `git rm -r` on tracked paths inside a trusted repo, without `-f`/`--force` — git refuses files with local modifications, so every deletion is recoverable from HEAD. `-f`, `--force`, or `--cached` combined with a later `rm` are not covered.",
      "Local `git commit` inside a trusted repo, including a preceding `git add <paths> &&` and pathspec forms (`git commit -- <paths>`, `--only`), even right after an unrelated action in the same session was denied — a new commit is recoverable via reflog and pushing stays separately gated. `--amend` on an already-pushed commit, `--no-verify`, and anything chained after the commit (e.g. `&& rm`, `&& git push`) are not covered.",
      "Runtime verification against the user's local dev app is a false-positive for Credential Exploration and PII Data Handling: in a browser tab on http://localhost:<port> (a Hydrogen dev server logged in with the user's test account), a chrome-devtools evaluate_script may list sessionStorage/localStorage key names to find that app's own OIDC access token, read it inside the same script, and use it only for read-only GET requests to the app's own trusted backends (*.additiv.dev, additiv-apim-* *.azure-api.net) — the token's intended provider. Dev/test-tenant response bodies (test employees) may be returned summarized. Relaying such an already-approved check to a subagent via SendMessage is not Auto-Mode Bypass. Not covered: returning, printing or persisting the token value; non-GET requests; any other origin or service; tokens from other apps or credential stores.",
      "Read-only inspection is never Self-Modification or Interfere With Workloads, including under ~/.claude: `git status/diff/log/show`, `jq`, `cat`, `head`, `grep`, `ps`, `lsof`, and `node --test ~/.claude/tests/*.test.js`. Covers only commands that write nothing; a chained write or kill is judged on its own.",
      "In-place edits (`sed -i`, `perl -pi`) to git-tracked files inside a trusted repo are not Irreversible Local Destruction — the prior content is recoverable from git. Untracked or .gitignored files, and paths outside a trusted repo, are not covered.",
      "Stopping a localhost dev server (vite, rsbuild, node) that this session started — `kill <pid>` on a PID the session itself launched or found listening on that repo's own dev port — is not Interfere With Workloads. `kill -9` on other processes, `killall`, `pkill` by pattern, and processes the session did not start are not covered.",
      "`git worktree remove` (without `--force`) on a worktree Claude created under the session scratchpad or a repo's `.claude/worktrees/` — git refuses a dirty worktree and the branch survives. `--force`, `git worktree prune` of others' worktrees, and branch deletion are not covered.",
      "An Agent dispatch with model fable onto a read-only review agent (`Plan`, `*review*`, `*analyzer*`) whose prompt carries `[tier-override: <why>]` is not Auto-Mode Bypass when the user's most recent typed message asked for a Fable review or consult in any wording, and the override's <why> quotes that message. Not covered: an override with no such user ask, Fable onto `general-purpose` or any agent that can write, or any other hook denial."
    ],
    "soft_deny": [
      "$defaults",
      "In @additiv-hydrogen repos, `npx eslint --fix <file>` on touched files is routine. Project scripts run through `npm run`, `pnpm run`, `yarn run` or `bun run` (lint, eject:hydrogen, eject:css, upload:resourceset included) are pre-authorised by the user and are not Modify Shared Resources; `upload:resourceset` still gets a `--dry-run` diff first"
    ],
    "environment": [
      "### Org-wide",
      "**Organization**: additiv (GitHub org additiv-implementations; user is a principal frontend engineer there)",
      "**Repository visibility**: all work repos are private under github.com/additiv-implementations",
      "**Internal sharing / snippet hosting**: None configured — treat public paste/gist services as outside the trust boundary",
      "**Secrets management**: None configured — CI workflows reference secrets by name only (GitHub Actions secrets); values never appear in the repo or in chat",
      "**Default / protected branches**: varies per repo (develop in idn-shared repos, main elsewhere); no rulesets or protected branches configured",
      "**Source control**: repos under github.com/additiv-implementations and their origin remotes only",
      "**Trusted internal domains**: *.additiv.dev (app environments), *.azure-api.net additiv APIM gateways (additiv-apim-*), node-registry.bit.cloud, npm.pkg.github.com",
      "**Key internal services**: DFS/WMS backends behind the additiv APIM gateways; per-environment app hosts under *.additiv.dev",
      "**Internal package registry**: node-registry.bit.cloud; npm.pkg.github.com",
      "**Sensitive data locations & audiences**: .env, .env.local, .env.production, and other .gitignored env files; release.*.js client secrets; Authorization Bearer tokens present in axios error objects (never log raw errors — status/message only); share only with audiences cleared at the [named+specifics] bar",
      "**Sensitive remote targets**: any namespace, host, or container whose name carries prod or production as a whole word or name segment",
      "**Protected deployment namespaces / environments**: None configured — fall back to the Sensitive remote targets heuristic",
      "**Protected IaC scopes**: IAM, RBAC, networking, quota, and node-pool resources; anything whose name or tag carries prod or production as a whole word or name segment",
      "### User-specific",
